1
00:00:00,060 --> 00:00:03,872
Before you pay a supplier, three documents should agree.

2
00:00:03,992 --> 00:00:06,017
It's called a three-way match.

3
00:00:06,137 --> 00:00:11,272
Purchase order, goods received note, supplier invoice.

4
00:00:11,392 --> 00:00:14,242
The order says 100 units.

5
00:00:14,362 --> 00:00:16,769
The store received 90.

6
00:00:16,889 --> 00:00:19,427
But the invoice bills 100.

7
00:00:19,547 --> 00:00:23,520
Pay it as it is, and you pay for 10 units you never got.

8
00:00:23,640 --> 00:00:30,214
Oracle and many ERPs can hold an invoice until all three agree.

9
00:00:30,334 --> 00:00:34,721
Want it set up to catch this? Send us a WhatsApp.
